Well, I'd finally gotten to the point where I thought I was ready for
Master Kaen. I'd found one potion of gain level and made another, and
drank them both as soon as I hit level 15 (the blessed one second, of
course :), and a nice few rounds of nurse dancing had given me a bonus
25-30 hp; I was sitting at 138, my first time in the triple digits.
Without any more scrolls of enchant armor, or magic markers, my AC was
still -17, but I had haste self and protection. I was wearing boots of
speed; between that and haste self I should have had him matched. AoR and
rings of regeneration and teleport control (two wands and two blessed
scrolls of the latter) rounded out the defense.

For offense I still had a bunch of blessed +5 darts and wands of
lightning, MM, slow monster, and cancellation. I'd had sleep memorized
with a couple potions for backup, ditto three potions of paralysis, plus
three bear traps and a land mine. It was the first time I'd ever faced
him, but I walked in with a cunning plan.

I take great pride in just how long my cunning plan took to fall apart.

Protection, haste self, and down the stairs. Plan A: zap sleep as soon as
I'm down. Plan B: um, line of sight on the big purple question mark is two
steps away; step step, zap sleep, and the purple question mark is in
motion anyway. Okay, plan C: zap teleport, jump to one of the little
islands in the lava.

So now I'm like the characters in _Aliens_, looking for little blips in my
peripheral vision. No chance I'm going to remove reflection to put on an
AoESP, so I have to wait. Suddenly Master Kaen is right beside me. Thump
thump open wounds. That's when I notice that I'm not on an island, there's
a ring of land around the level. *And* I'm down 40hp on his first strike.
Maybe I was not ready for this. Blessed port! Where do you want to go?
Level 1. Let me retrace my steps, see the priest in Minetown again, get a
few more things out of the ache I left in Soko.... Nope. I didn't realize
I'd end up on QUEST level 1. Doh!

Throw paralysis and make for the stairs. No, not the portal; like a dope I
make for the stairs. Why? because I left a bunch of loot down there to be
unencumbered, some of which could help me against Kaen, I'm still
thinking. And also because I don't want him waiting right in my face the
next time I come through the portal. I make it to the stairs, but he's
with me in the end. We go down together. Can't go up, let me get to my
Elberethed cache. Teleport down to level 3 (Now the count of blessed teep
scrolls is 0.)

And he's still attached to my hip. So I have to make a stand, and throw a
sleep potion at him, and he nods off. In the course of my throwing darts
at him, though, suddenly he disappeared! No reading of scrolls, no zapping
of wands, just disappears. He can teleport!? Suddenly I've got a harrier.
He blips in, gives me a couple punches, and when I counterpunch he blips
out. He gives me just enough time - *almost* - to regenerate between
smackarounds. I counter by standing on the downstairs where I can rest
between rounds; but then so can he. Obviously, I need to limit the number
of squares he can blip into, so I take my traps into a corner and ring
myself. ("Obviously" hah! Obvisouly I needed to just get the hell out.)

So, let's move on to the traps - he didn't trip them. Bop in, stand on a
bear trap or a mine that didn't go off, and bop out. Is that an intrinsic
part of teleportation, was he possibly wearing a ring of free action, or
is his dex just that high?

I make a run for the stairs, but he's there. and this time he doesn't port
away. I get stomped. Zap teleport to the downstairs, he comes with me but
I can still barely escape. It's going to be very hard to try that trick
again.

Tanned rested, and unready, I come topside again. zap teleport to go
directly to the stairs. He's *on* them. Because I'd had almost no trouble
with the xorn, I never thought to use the E word on my escape route.

But really, I never knew he could teleport....

